    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "542:3037",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Classroom",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Classroom"
        },
        {
          "text": "My English Classroom\n\nOur English classroom is on the second floor of the school building. It is a bright, spacious room with large windows that let in plenty of natural light.\n\nAt the front of the room, there is a whiteboard where the teacher writes vocabulary and grammar rules. Next to it, there is a projector screen that the teacher uses for presentations and videos. The teacher's desk sits in the corner with a laptop, a stack of textbooks, and a cup of pens and markers.\n\nThe students sit at individual desks arranged in rows. Each desk has a drawer for storing notebooks, pencils, and erasers. Some students keep a pencil case with highlighters, a ruler, and a sharpener. There is a bookshelf at the back of the room filled with dictionaries, readers, and reference books.\n\nOn the walls, there are posters with grammar charts, a world map, and a bulletin board where the teacher pins student work and important notices. A clock on the wall helps everyone keep track of time during lessons.\n\nThe classroom also has a cupboard where supplies are kept: paper, scissors, glue, tape, and folders. Near the door, there is a recycling bin and a regular bin for rubbish.\n\nDuring lessons, the teacher often asks us to work in pairs or groups. We move our chairs together and discuss topics, complete worksheets, or practise dialogues. I enjoy our classroom — it is where I started to feel confident speaking English.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "My English Classroom Our English classroom is on the second floor of the school building. It is a bright, spacious room with large windows that let in plenty of natural light. At the front of the room, there is a whiteboard where the teacher writes vocabulary and grammar rules. Next to it, there is a projector screen that the teacher uses for presentations and videos. The teacher's desk sits in the corner with a laptop, a stack of textbooks, and a cup of pens and markers. The students sit at individual desks arranged in rows. Each desk has a drawer for storing notebooks, pencils, and erasers. Some students keep a pencil case with highlighters, a ruler, and a sharpener. There is a bookshelf at the back of the room filled with dictionaries, readers, and reference books. On the walls, there are posters with grammar charts, a world map, and a bulletin board where the teacher pins student work and important notices. A clock on the wall helps everyone keep track of time during lessons. The classroom also has a cupboard where supplies are kept: paper, scissors, glue, tape, and folders. Near the door, there is a recycling bin and a regular bin for rubbish. During lessons, the teacher often asks us to work in pairs or groups. We move our chairs together and discuss topics, complete worksheets, or practise dialogues. I enjoy our classroom — it is where I started to feel confident speaking English."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. Where is the classroom located in the school?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. Where is the classroom located in the school?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. What does the teacher use the projector screen for?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. What does the teacher use the projector screen for?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What can students find on the bookshelf?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What can students find on the bookshelf?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. What is displayed on the bulletin board?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. What is displayed on the bulletin board?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. How do students work together during lessons?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. How do students work together during lessons?"
        }
      ]
    },
    "idioms-phrases": {
      "nodeId": "542:3050",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases"
        },
        {
          "text": "hit the books",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "hit the books"
        },
        {
          "text": "start studying seriously",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "start studying seriously"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The exam is tomorrow — grab your textbook, notebook, and highlighter and hit the books.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The exam is tomorrow — grab your textbook, notebook, and highlighter and hit the books.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "learn the ropes",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "learn the ropes"
        },
        {
          "text": "learn the basics of how something works",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "learn the basics of how something works"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"On the first day, the new student learned the ropes — where to find the locker, the shelf, and the bulletin board.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"On the first day, the new student learned the ropes — where to find the locker, the shelf, and the bulletin board.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "by the book",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "by the book"
        },
        {
          "text": "following rules exactly",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "following rules exactly"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The teacher does everything by the book — every pencil in the pencil case, every folder in the binder.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The teacher does everything by the book — every pencil in the pencil case, every folder in the binder.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "make the grade",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "make the grade"
        },
        {
          "text": "meet the required standard; succeed",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "meet the required standard; succeed"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"She studied with the dictionary and the workbook every night and finally made the grade.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"She studied with the dictionary and the workbook every night and finally made the grade.\""
        },
        {
